  "description": {
    "raw": "A black ray projects from your pointing finger. You must succeed on a ranged touch attack with the ray to strike a target.\n\nThe subject is immediately exhausted for the spell's duration. A successful Fortitude save means the creature is only fatigued.\n\nA character that is already fatigued instead becomes exhausted.\n\nThis spell has no effect on a creature that is already exhausted. Unlike normal exhaustion or fatigue, the effect ends as soon as the spell's duration expires.",
    "search_text": "\"a black ray projects from your pointing finger. you must succeed on a ranged touch attack with the ray to strike a target.\\n\\nthe subject is immediately exhausted for the spell's duration. a successful fortitude save means the creature is only fatigued.\\n\\na character that is already fatigued instead becomes exhausted.\\n\\nthis spell has no effect on a creature that is already exhausted. unlike normal exhaustion or fatigue, the effect ends as soon as the spell's duration expires.\"",
